Furthermore, once these paths are created, our subconscious travels them whether we like it or not. They may even form new paths without us knowing -- shortcuts to feelings whose origins are then forgotten, the result of countless choices that we made sometime in the past.8 (I once had a friend who trimmed her[ nails] to calm herself down. She[ picked] up the habit by being calm, then trimming her[ nails]). Even our emotions can[ manifest] as these “un[conscious] habits.” 9 Let me say that again: our emotions can be habits whose origins we’ve forgotten.
