> Seane[ Corn] and Colleen Saidman Yee explore how yoga gives us the tools to make mindful decisions and change the world.
[Rod]ney Yee explains his teaching philosophy, how yoga empowers him to directly touch life, and what he thinks is the most important thing to ask a new student.
Kino MacGregor discusses how the different roles played by home practice and study with teachers combine in our own personal yoga journeys.
Elena[ Brow]er shares her philosophy with Beryl Bender[ Birch], from the one sutra every new teacher needs, to her hope for asana in the world.
